<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-Russian Convention</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1907">1907</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-Russian Convention was an agreement of 1907 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> settling their rivalries in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>. It divided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> into spheres of influence and recognised British influence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and the neutrality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>. It eased the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-great-game">Great Game</a>' and helped form the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/triple-entente">Triple Entente</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-russian-convention.jpg" alt="Anglo-Russian Convention" width="320" height="266" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fabienkhan · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Iran_1900-en.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
